{
  "info": {
    "name": "LIMS — Method",
    "description": "Method master-data REST API. JWT Bearer auth (ADR-009). Run \"Login as admin\" first to seed {{accessToken}}.\n\nDual-shape (same pattern as Source, Unit, Test):\n  FLAT     LIST / CREATE → /api/methods         (used by master-data /methods page; nested test → category included in list rows)\n  NESTED   LIST / CREATE → /api/tests/:testID/methods\n  ITEM     GET / PUT / DELETE → /api/methods/:methodID\n\nPREREQUISITE: A valid Test must exist. Set {{testID}} in collection variables to a real test UUID before running (run Test collection first, then copy the testID).\n\nRun top-to-bottom: POST seeds {{methodID}} which subsequent requests reuse.\n\nisDefault swap test: a second method created with isDefault=true must flip the first method to isDefault=false. Verifies single-default-per-test enforcement (works on flat POST too — same transaction logic).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3033/api",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@lims.local",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "Admin123",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "testID",
      "value": "REPLACE_WITH_VALID_TEST_UUID",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "methodID",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "method2ID",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Content-Type', value: 'application/json' });",
          "const path = pm.request.url.getPath();",
          "const isLogin = /\\/auth\\/login$/.test(path);",
          "if (!isLogin) {",
          "  const token = pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken');",
          "  if (token) pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: 'Bearer ' + token });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Login as admin (seeds {{accessToken}})",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "auth",
            "login"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.data.accessToken);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List methods (flat — master-data view, all tests)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods?page=1&limit=20&sort=createdAt&order=desc",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods"
          ],
          "query": [
            { "key": "page",      "value": "1" },
            { "key": "limit",     "value": "20" },
            { "key": "sort",      "value": "createdAt" },
            { "key": "order",     "value": "desc" },
            { "key": "search",    "value": "",     "disabled": true },
            { "key": "testID",    "value": "",     "disabled": true },
            { "key": "isDefault", "value": "true", "disabled": true },
            { "key": "isActive",  "value": "true", "disabled": true }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Flat list across all tests. Each row includes a `test` association ({ testID, name, categoryID, category: { categoryID, name, type } }) so the master-data UI can render Test name + parent Category without extra round-trips."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=true', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('data is array', () => pm.expect(body.data).to.be.an('array'));",
              "pm.test('meta has total/page/limit/totalPages', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.meta).to.have.all.keys('total','page','limit','totalPages');",
              "});",
              "if (body.data.length > 0) {",
              "  pm.test('row includes nested test → category association', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(body.data[0].test).to.be.an('object');",
              "    pm.expect(body.data[0].test).to.have.property('name');",
              "  });",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Create method (flat — testID in body)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"testID\": \"{{testID}}\",\n  \"code\": \"ISO 2719\",\n  \"description\": \"Determination of flash point — Pensky-Martens closed cup method.\",\n  \"isDefault\": false,\n  \"isActive\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Flat create — used by the master-data /methods page. The `testID` is in the body (not URL). Backend verifies the parent test exists; returns 404 if not. PUT does NOT accept `testID` (cannot move a method to a different test). If `isDefault=true`, all sibling defaults are flipped off in the same transaction."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=true', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('data.methodID present', () => pm.expect(body.data.methodID).to.be.a('string'));",
              "pm.test('testID matches body', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.testID).to.eql(pm.variables.get('testID'));",
              "});",
              "pm.test('description persisted', () => pm.expect(body.data.description).to.be.a('string'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "List methods for test",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tests/{{testID}}/methods?page=1&limit=20&sort=createdAt&order=desc",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "tests",
            "{{testID}}",
            "methods"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "page",
              "value": "1"
            },
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "20"
            },
            {
              "key": "sort",
              "value": "createdAt"
            },
            {
              "key": "order",
              "value": "desc"
            },
            {
              "key": "search",
              "value": "",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "isDefault",
              "value": "true",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "isActive",
              "value": "true",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=true', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('data is array', () => pm.expect(body.data).to.be.an('array'));",
              "pm.test('meta has total/page/limit/totalPages', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.meta).to.have.all.keys('total','page','limit','totalPages');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Create method (isDefault=true)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"ASTM D93-25\",\n  \"description\": \"Flash Point by Pensky-Martens Closed Cup\",\n  \"isDefault\": true,\n  \"isActive\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tests/{{testID}}/methods",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "tests",
            "{{testID}}",
            "methods"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=true', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('data.methodID present', () => pm.expect(body.data.methodID).to.be.a('string'));",
              "pm.test('testID matches', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.testID).to.eql(pm.variables.get('testID'));",
              "});",
              "pm.test('isDefault=true', () => pm.expect(body.data.isDefault).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('audit fields populated', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.createdBy).to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.updatedBy).to.be.a('string');",
              "});",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('methodID', body.data.methodID);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Create duplicate code in same test (case-insensitive — expect 409)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"astm d93-25\",\n  \"isDefault\": false,\n  \"isActive\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tests/{{testID}}/methods",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "tests",
            "{{testID}}",
            "methods"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Verifies the (testID, LOWER(code)) unique partial index. 'astm d93-25' must collide with 'ASTM D93-25' within the same test."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=false', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.false);",
              "pm.test('message indicates unique violation', () => pm.expect(body.message).to.match(/unique|duplicate/i));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get method by ID",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods/{{methodID}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods",
            "{{methodID}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=true', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('matches requested ID', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.methodID).to.eql(pm.variables.get('methodID'));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Update method (PUT — set isDefault=false)",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"ASTM D93-25\",\n  \"description\": \"Flash Point by Pensky-Martens Closed Cup (updated)\",\n  \"isDefault\": false,\n  \"isActive\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods/{{methodID}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods",
            "{{methodID}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=true', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('isDefault=false', () => pm.expect(body.data.isDefault).to.be.false);",
              "pm.test('description updated', () => pm.expect(body.data.description).to.include('updated'));",
              "pm.test('updatedBy populated', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.updatedBy).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Create second method (isDefault=true — verify sibling swap)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"code\": \"IP 34\",\n  \"description\": \"Flash Point by Abel Closed Cup\",\n  \"isDefault\": true,\n  \"isActive\": true\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/tests/{{testID}}/methods",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "tests",
            "{{testID}}",
            "methods"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates a second method with isDefault=true. Controller must reset the first method ({{methodID}}) to isDefault=false in the same transaction. Verified by request #7."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=true', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.true);",
              "pm.test('isDefault=true on new method', () => pm.expect(body.data.isDefault).to.be.true);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('method2ID', body.data.methodID);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Verify first method isDefault=false after swap",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods/{{methodID}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods",
            "{{methodID}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "After request #6 set method2 as default, this GET confirms the first method was automatically flipped to isDefault=false by the transaction."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('isDefault=false (sibling was reset by transaction)', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.isDefault).to.be.false;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Soft delete second method (cleanup)",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods/{{method2ID}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods",
            "{{method2ID}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Soft delete method",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods/{{methodID}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods",
            "{{methodID}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204 No Content', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));",
              "pm.test('empty body', () => pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.have.lengthOf(0));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get deleted method (expect 404)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/methods/{{methodID}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "methods",
            "{{methodID}}"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('404 Not Found', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('success=false', () => pm.expect(body.success).to.be.false);",
              "pm.test('message references Method', () => pm.expect(body.message).to.match(/Method/i));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
